---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Veloce Tools"
  description="How Veloce Tools handles data: what runs locally in your browser, what (if anything) touches our servers, and how ads and analytics work."
>
  <section class="section--tight prose">
    <div class="tool-hero">
      <h1 style="font-size:40px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
    </div>

    <h2>What runs in your browser</h2>
    <p>Most tools on Veloce Tools — password generation, hashing, UUIDs, Base64/URL encoding, JSON formatting, text counting, color conversion, image compression and conversion — run entirely in your browser using JavaScript. That content is never sent to our servers, and we have no record of what you typed or uploaded into those tools.</p>

    <h2>What does touch our servers</h2>
    <p>Some tools (such as anything that checks a live website) require a server-side request to work, since browsers can't read most external sites directly. Where that's the case, the tool's own page says so, and the request is discarded immediately after — nothing is logged against your visit.</p>

    <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
    <p>We may use standard web analytics to understand aggregate traffic (which pages are used, roughly how much traffic we get) and, over time, may run advertising through a network such as Google AdSense. Ad networks and analytics providers may use cookies or similar technologies to serve relevant ads and measure performance. You can control cookies through your browser settings, and opt out of personalized advertising through <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration:underline;">Google's Ads Settings</a>.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Veloce Tools is built and maintained by <a href="https://velocedigital.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration:underline;">Veloce Digital</a>. For questions about this policy, reach out via the contact page on velocedigital.co.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
